<p>Nueces County's larger totals partly reflect its larger population and more observers, not only more storms. In every county, May is the leading month for both hail and thunderstorm wind reports. For local context, see our pages for <a href="/service-areas/rockport-tx/">Rockport</a> and <a href="/service-areas/kingsville-tx/">Kingsville</a>.</p>

<h2>What this history means for your claim</h2>

<p>Storm history explains risk; it does not prove a particular loss. If you suspect damage, check the reports for your date and area with our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a> or the <a href="/storm-history/">storm history</a> page, then document the property itself with photos, measurements, and an inspection. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster, serving Corpus Christi, Nueces County, and surrounding Coastal Bend communities, can help assemble that record and present the claim. We cannot promise a result, and coverage depends on your policy. Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement.</p>
